1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,830
The most dangerous thing in the world still lies beneath Chernobyl.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:08,110
In 1986, the reactor core melted.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:11,890
Fuel, sand and concrete fused into lava.

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:15,390
That lava flowed into the rooms below, and set solid.

5
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:21,050
Months later, workers found it. It was shaped like an elephant's foot.

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,310
It got its name: the Elephant's Foot.

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:28,450
At first, standing near it for just five minutes was enough to kill you.

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,910
No one could get close, so a camera was sent in on wheels.

9
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:37,510
Today it is weaker than before, but it is still deadly.

10
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:40,790
And for the next hundred years, it will stay under this arch.

11
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:46,890
The full documentary is on this channel. Tap the link below to watch it.

